# BigYellow Beacon — shared context (read before any task)

## Product in one paragraph
BigYellow Beacon is an **offline-first AI copilot for seafarers' wellbeing and safety**, built by Bigyellowfish (BYF) for the Google Cloud AI Builder Cup 2026. Merchant ships have little or no internet. Crew use a phone app on the **ship's Wi-Fi** to (a) report hazards / near-misses by voice, photo or text in their own language, and (b) do a 60-second daily wellbeing check-in. An **edge server on the ship** runs **Gemma 3n offline** and serves the crew app and the Master's dashboard. When the ship's VSAT link is up, the edge server syncs a small delta (~1 KB) to **shore on Google Cloud**, where **Gemini** finds patterns across the fleet (e.g. the same crane hydraulic leak on 3 sister vessels), links them to past accident cases, and sends fleet alerts and an enriched morning brief back to the ship.

## Three kinds of users
| User | App | Talks to |
|---|---|---|
| Crew member (`crew`) | Android app (`mobile/android`, built in Codex) | Edge server only |
| Master / Safety Officer (`master`, `safety_officer`) | Ship dashboard (`dashboards/ship-web`), served by the edge server on the ship LAN | Edge server only |
| Shore management (`shore_safety`, `shore_psych`, `admin`) | Shore dashboard (`dashboards/shore-web`) on Firebase Hosting | Shore API |

## Architecture
```
Crew app ──ship Wi-Fi──▶ EDGE (FastAPI + Gemma 3n + faster-whisper + EmbeddingGemma + Postgres/pgvector)
Ship dashboard ──LAN──▶ EDGE (same origin, served at /)
EDGE sync worker ──VSAT, only when up──▶ SHORE shore-api (Cloud Run) ──▶ Firestore (+ vector search), Gemini (Vertex AI), Cloud Storage
Shore dashboard (Firebase Hosting + Firebase Auth) ──▶ shore-api
```
Everything on the ship must keep working with the link down. The **only** thing crossing ship↔shore is the sync worker.

